<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mermnad dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 680–547 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> · Also known as Mermnads</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mermnad dynasty ruled the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydia">Lydia</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardis">Sardis</a> from about 680 BCE until the Persian conquest around 547 BCE. Its kings, Gyges, Ardys, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sadyattes">Sadyattes</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alyattes">Alyattes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croesus">Croesus</a>, subdued most of the Greek cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionia">Ionia</a>, fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimmerians">Cimmerians</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a>, and issued the first coins. Croesus, the last of them, was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a>.</p></div>
